Findings are ready. Summary of what I did: read the diff and enclosing handler, traced the constants (`ASTRO_PATH_PARAM`, `ISR_PATH`, `buildISRFolder`, `allowQuery`) in `index.ts`, compared against the prior security hardening commit (#15959) and its test, ran the adapter's `path-override-security` and `isr` tests (pass), ran biome on the changed file (format error), and probed the built `_render` and `_isr` handlers in-process from a scratch script. The probe confirmed that a client-supplied `x-vercel-isr: 1` header plus `?x_astro_path=` re-enables the path override on `_render` (`/api/public` returned `{"id":"private"}`), and that `isr.exclude`d routes (`/two`, `/api/foo`) are rendered by the `_isr` function via `/_isr?x_astro_path=...`. Per the run policy I did not read AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, so the conventions angle yields nothing.

